Notebook[
 {Cell["Proton-proton classes, step 2 (Tracer route): spin and colour \
algebra", "Title"], Cell["Same task, same input and same output as \
2-Algebra-FeynCalc.wl; read its introduction first, which defines the three \
parts of the output (Born, Virtual, Real), the invariants s, t, u, A, B, C, \
spe3 and the scalar-integral families of the one-loop interference.  Here the \
Dirac and Lorentz algebra is done by the classic Tracer package (M. Jamin and \
M. E. Lautenbacher, Comput. Phys. Commun. 74 (1993) 265), and the colour \
algebra by an explicit SU(N) reduction written out in this file.  Input: the \
amplitude records of step 1 (Results/class-<n>/Amplitudes.wl, key \
\"Records\").  Output: Results/Tracer/class-<n>/Algebra.wl, which the last \
cell compares exactly with Results/FeynCalc/class-<n>/Algebra.wl.  Run this \
file in a fresh kernel: Tracer and FeynCalc cannot be loaded \
together.\n\nSpin sums (HVBM scheme for LL), as in the FeynCalc route.  The \
physical momenta pa, pb, p are four-dimensional; the unobserved k1, k2 and \
the loop momentum have (D-4)-dimensional (\"hatted\") parts.  Incoming quark: \
p-slash/2 (UU) or +-p-slash gamma5/2 (LL; plus for a quark, minus for an \
antiquark, since u ubar = p-slash (1 + h gamma5)/2 and v vbar = p-slash (1 - \
h gamma5)/2 for a massless fermion of helicity h); the factor 1/2 is part of \
the average below.  Incoming gluon: the physical polarization sum averaged \
with 1/(D-2) (UU), or the circular density (LL), which already contains the \
factor 1/2 of the helicity difference.  Outgoing gluons: the physical sum \
-g^{mu nu} + (l^mu r^nu + r^mu l^nu)/(l.r) with a reference vector \
r.\n\nTracer's vocabulary (summarized in FeynFacet/Tracer.wl and introduced \
in Processes/LeptonQuark/2-Algebra-Tracer.wl):\n  G[line, p, {mu}, ...]   the \
string p-slash gamma^mu ... on a fermion line; it is a trace once Spur[line] \
has been declared; G5 inside it is gamma5;\n  S[p, q] = p.q,  S[p, {mu}] = \
p^mu,  S[{mu}, {nu}] = g^{mu nu}  (D-dimensional); an index that occurs twice \
in an expanded product is contracted automatically, also when the other \
occurrence is inside any expression f[..., {mu}, ...]: S[{mu}, p] f[..., \
{mu}, ...] = f[..., p, ...];\n  H[p, q]   the hatted, (D-4)-dimensional part \
of p.q;\n  Eps[a, b, c, d]   the four-dimensional epsilon tensor (Tracer \
stores it internally as eps[{a, b, c, d}]);\n  VectorDimension[D]   \
D-dimensional vectors and gamma matrices;  AntiCommute[off]   the HVBM \
gamma5, which anticommutes with the four-dimensional gamma matrices and \
commutes with the hatted ones.\n\nSign of the epsilon tensor.  Tracer defines \
gamma5 = (i/4!) eps_{mu nu rho sigma} gamma^mu gamma^nu gamma^rho \
gamma^sigma, so that Tr[gamma5 a-slash b-slash c-slash d-slash] = +4 i Eps[a, \
b, c, d]: the opposite sign to FeynCalc with $LeviCivitaSign = -1.  The \
circular density of a polarized incoming gluon of momentum l, i eps^{mu nu l \
r}/(2 l.r) in the FeynCalc route, therefore reads -i Eps[mu, nu, l, r]/(2 \
l.r) here.  This sign is tested by the Born squares, which contain a gamma5 \
and a circular density together in the q g channels and two circular \
densities in the g g channels.", "Text"], Cell["Load", "Section"], 
  Cell["The FeynFacet package (file locations, the record format, the checks \
Require[...]) and then Tracer.", "Text"], Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDir\
ectory[], \"..\", \"..\", \"FeynFacet\", \"FeynFacet.wl\"}]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Tracer itself.  It redefines Dot and NonCommutativeMultiply on \
startup; LoadTracer restores them, so that ordinary Mathematica expressions \
keep working.", "Text"], Cell["LoadTracer[]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Choices: the class; the number of parallel kernels for the squares \
(\"auto\" = one per processor core, at most 8; \"1\" = none); and whether the \
pair files of an earlier run of this same, unchanged file may be reused \
(\"no\" recomputes everything; \"yes\" only continues an interrupted run: a \
product file is reused only if its companion file <name>.input holds the \
fingerprint of the current inputs, the amplitudes of step 1 and this step \
file; a file written for other inputs, or without that companion (for \
example, after an interrupted write), is computed again).\n\nThe records were \
written in step 1 by a kernel with FeynCalc loaded, in which the number of \
light flavours is FeynCalc's symbol Nf (context FeynCalc`); it is renamed to \
the plain symbol Nf of the FeynCalc route's output.  Tracer is set to D \
dimensions with the HVBM gamma5, and the lines 1, 2, 3 are declared traces: \
lines 1 and 2 for the (at most two) traces formed by closing the open quark \
lines of an interference, line 3 for a closed quark loop of a one-loop \
graph.", "Text"], Cell["class = \"13\";\nworkers = \"auto\";\nresume = \
\"no\";\nloaded = LoadAmplitudes[\"class-\" <> class];\nplainNf = \
Thread[Select[Union[Cases[loaded, _Symbol, Infinity, Heads -> True]], \
SymbolName[#] === \"Nf\" && Context[#] =!= \"Global`\" &] -> Nf];\nrecords = \
loaded[\"Records\"] /. plainNf; spec = loaded[\"Spec\"] /. plainNf; weights = \
loaded[\"Weights\"] /. \
plainNf;\nVectorDimension[D];\nAntiCommute[off];\nSpur[1, 2, 3];\nspec", 
   "Input"], Cell["The first record of the first diagram of each part, as an \
example of the input: a coefficient (couplings, colour factors ColorT, \
ColorF, ColorDelta, GluonDelta, propagators Den[q] = 1/q^2, metric tensors, \
momentum components, polarization vectors PolVector[l, mu, +1 incoming / -1 \
outgoing]) and the open fermion chains Chain[Ubar or Vbar, gamma matrices, \
Uspinor or Vspinor].  A one-loop record with a closed quark loop also has \
\"Traces\": the loop's Dirac trace, a string of gamma matrices, which is \
traced.  Legacy records also list there the other factors of the loop \
(numbers, couplings, generators) as separate entries; these multiply.  \
Everything FeynArts attaches to the closed loop (its sign, the factor Nf of \
the flavours in it) is already part of the record.", "Text"], 
  Cell["ShowRecords[Join[If[records[\"Born\"] === {}, {}, \
{records[\"Born\"][[1, 1]]}], {First[First[records[\"Real\"]]][[1]]}]]", 
   "Input"], Cell["The QCD amplitudes contain only gamma^mu and slashed \
momenta, no gamma5 (the gamma5 of the LL spin sums is inserted below).  This \
matters for the complex conjugation below, which reverses a gamma string; \
that is the Dirac adjoint only for gamma^mu and slashed momenta (gamma0 \
gamma5^dagger gamma0 = -gamma5 would need a sign).", "Text"], 
  Cell["Require[FreeQ[records, GammaFive], \"A record contains gamma5; the \
conjugation below does not handle it\"];\n\"no gamma5 in the amplitudes\"", 
   "Input"], Cell["Conventions", "Section"], Cell["Incoming partons and \
averages, as in the FeynCalc route: a quark is averaged with 1/(2 Nc) (spin \
and colour), a gluon with 1/((D-2)(Nc^2-1)) for UU and 1/(Nc^2-1) for LL (the \
1/2 of the helicity difference is in the circular density); \
polarizedQuarkSign is +1 for a quark and -1 for an antiquark.  colourFactors \
writes the result with CA = Nc and CF = (Nc^2-1)/(2 Nc).\n\nKinematics are \
installed by functions, because every parallel kernel installs them for each \
job; they are always called inside Internal`InheritedBlock[{S, H}, ...], \
which keeps the declared scalar products local to one job while retaining \
Tracer's own rules for S and H.  The physical momenta pa, pb, p have no \
hatted components (H = 0; H is also made linear, since Tracer leaves H of a \
momentum sum unexpanded).  In the real emission the unobserved k1 and k2 have \
the hatted products H[k1, k1] = H[k2, k2] = -H[k1, k2] = spe3 (k1hat = \
-k2hat, since the physical momenta have no hatted parts); in the Born and \
one-loop kinematics k1 is four-dimensional too, and the loop momentum keeps \
its hatted part, H[loop, loop] = loopHat2 (see the one-loop section).  Inside \
the amplitudes k1 = pa + pb - p (Born and one loop) and k2 = pa + pb - p - k1 \
(real) are eliminated, except in the spinors, whose spin sums give the \
slashed momentum itself.", "Text"], Cell["incoming = (spec[\"Born\"] /. None \
-> spec[\"Real\"][[1, 1]])[[1 ;; 2]];       (* the two incoming partons \
*)\npolarizedQuarkSign = <|pa -> If[StringEndsQ[incoming[[1]], \"b\"], -1, \
1], pb -> If[StringEndsQ[incoming[[2]], \"b\"], -1, 1]|>;\nincomingGluons = \
Select[{pa, pb}, incoming[[Position[{pa, pb}, #][[1, 1]]]] === \"g\" \
&];\nincomingQuarks = Complement[{pa, pb}, \
incomingGluons];\naverage[spinCase_] := Times @@ (Switch[incoming[[#]], \
\"g\", If[spinCase === \"LL\", 1, 1/(D - 2)]/(Nc^2 - 1), _, 1/(2 Nc)] & /@ \
{1, 2});\ncolourFactors[expr_] := Factor[expr] /. (-1 + Nc) (1 + Nc) -> 2 Nc \
CF /. Nc -> CA;\n\ndeclare[products_List] := (Unprotect[S]; Scan[(S[#[[1]], \
#[[2]]] = #[[3]]) &, products]; Protect[S]);\nfourDimensional[momenta_List] \
:= (Unprotect[H];\n  H[x_, y_Plus] := H[x, #] & /@ y; H[x_Plus, y_] := H[#, \
y] & /@ x;\n  H[x_, c_?NumericQ y_] := c H[x, y]; H[c_?NumericQ x_, y_] := c \
H[x, y];\n  Scan[(H[#] = 0; H[#, _] = 0) &, momenta]; \
Protect[H]);\nbornKinematics := (fourDimensional[{pa, pb, p, k1}];\n  \
declare[{{pa, pa, 0}, {pb, pb, 0}, {p, p, 0}, {k1, k1, 0}, {pa, pb, s/2}, \
{pa, p, -t/2}, {pb, p, -u/2},\n    {pa, k1, -u/2}, {pb, k1, -t/2}, {p, k1, \
s/2}}]);\nrealKinematics := (fourDimensional[{pa, pb, p}];\n  Unprotect[H]; \
H[k1, k1] = spe3; H[k2, k2] = spe3; H[k1, k2] = -spe3; Protect[H];\n  \
declare[{{pa, pa, 0}, {pb, pb, 0}, {p, p, 0}, {k1, k1, 0}, {k2, k2, 0}, {pa, \
pb, s/2}, {pa, p, -t/2}, {pb, p, -u/2},\n    {pa, k1, -A/2}, {pb, k1, -B/2}, \
{p, k1, C/2}, {pa, k2, (s + t + A)/2}, {pb, k2, (s + u + B)/2}, {p, k2, (-t - \
u - C)/2},\n    {k1, k2, (s + t + u)/2}}]);\ninstallKinematics[name_] := \
If[name === \"Born\", bornKinematics, realKinematics];\nbornConservation = k1 \
-> pa + pb - p;\nrealConservation = k2 -> pa + pb - p - \
k1;\nconservedMomentum[rule_][q_] := Expand[q /. rule];      (* the map of \
momenta inside an amplitude: eliminate k1 or k2 *)\nepsHead = Head[Eps[a1, \
a2, a3, a4]];          (* Tracer's internal head of the epsilon tensor \
*)\n{incomingQuarks, incomingGluons, average[\"UU\"]}", "Input"], 
  Cell["Colour: an explicit SU(N) reduction", "Section"], 
  Cell["The colour factor of an interference is a closed colour network: the \
colour structure of a term of the amplitude times the complex conjugate of a \
colour structure of the other amplitude, all indices summed.  It is reduced \
with three identities, in the normalization Tr(T^a T^b) = delta^{ab}/2 of the \
FeynCalc route:\n\n  (1) structure constants as traces:  f^{abc} = -2 i ( \
Tr[T^a T^b T^c] - Tr[T^b T^a T^c] )   (from [T^a, T^b] = i f^{abc} T^c);\n  \
(2) the Fierz identity, which removes a summed gluon index:  (T^a)_{ij} \
(T^a)_{kl} = 1/2 ( delta_{il} delta_{kj} - delta_{ij} delta_{kl}/Nc );\n  (3) \
closed loops:  delta_{ii} = Nc,  Tr[T^a] = 0,  and delta^{aa} = Nc^2 - 1 for \
a gluon delta.\n\nNotation: generators[{a, b, ...}, i, j] = (T^a T^b \
...)_{ij} is a string of generators between the quark colours i and j \
(generators[{}, i, j] = delta_{ij}; a closed trace Tr[T^a T^b ...] is a \
string whose two ends carry the same summed index); adjointDelta[a, b] = \
delta^{ab}.  A network is first written in these objects: each ColorT is a \
string, each ColorDelta an empty string, each GluonDelta an adjointDelta, and \
each ColorF becomes, by (1), the difference of two closed traces with new \
summed quark indices (fresh names, one pair for every f, also when the same f \
occurs twice as f^{abc} f^{abc}).  Then the following rules are applied until \
nothing changes:\n\n  adjoint deltas: delta^{aa} = Nc^2 - 1, delta^{ab} \
delta^{ab} = Nc^2 - 1, delta^{ab} delta^{bc} = delta^{ac}, and delta^{ab} \
inside a string renames b to a;\n  closed loops (3): generators[{}, i, i] = \
Nc, generators[{a}, i, i] = 0, delta_{ij} delta_{ij} = Nc;\n  joining: a \
delta_{ij} next to a string renames the index; two strings that share a quark \
index j, (X)_{ij} (Y)_{jk} = (X Y)_{ik}, are joined into one;\n  the Fierz \
identity (2), for a gluon index a that occurs twice in one string or once in \
each of two strings:\n     generators[{X, a, Y, a, Z}, i, j] = 1/2 ( Tr[Y] \
generators[{X, Z}, i, j] - generators[{X, Y, Z}, i, j]/Nc ),\n     \
generators[{X, a, Y}, i, j] generators[{U, a, V}, k, l] = 1/2 ( \
generators[{X, V}, i, l] generators[{U, Y}, k, j] - generators[{X, Y}, i, j] \
generators[{U, V}, k, l]/Nc ).\n\nEvery application of (2) removes one gluon \
index, so the reduction ends with a polynomial in Nc and 1/Nc; a network that \
still contains a colour object afterwards is reported as a failure.  The \
complex conjugate of a colour structure transposes the generators, (T^a \
T^b)_{ij}^* = (T^b T^a)_{ji} (f and the deltas are real), and renames the \
indices summed inside it so that they cannot coincide with those of the \
amplitude.  Each distinct network is evaluated once and remembered \
(colourCache); networks that differ only by the names of their summed indices \
are recognized by a canonical renaming: the factors are sorted by their shape \
with the indices blanked out, and the indices are then numbered colour1, \
colour2, ... in order of first appearance.", "Text"], 
  Cell["colourHeads = ColorT | ColorF | ColorDelta | \
GluonDelta;\nfactorList[term_] := Flatten[Replace[If[Head[term] === Times, \
List @@ term, {term}], Power[x_, n_Integer?Positive] :> ConstantArray[x, n], \
{1}]];\ntermList[expr_] := If[Head[expr] === Plus, List @@ expr, \
{expr}];\ncolourIndices[colour_] := Flatten[factorList[colour] /. \
{ColorT[l_List, i_, j_] :> {l, i, j}, (ColorF | ColorDelta | GluonDelta)[x__] \
:> {x}, _?NumericQ -> {}}];\ninternalColour[colour_] := \
Select[Tally[colourIndices[colour]], #[[2]] > 1 &][[All, 1]];      (* the \
indices summed inside one colour structure *)\nconjugateColour[colour_] := \
colour /. Thread[internalColour[colour] -> (Symbol[\"c\" <> SymbolName[#]] & \
/@ internalColour[colour])] /.\n  ColorT[l_List, i_, j_] :> \
ColorT[Reverse[l], j, i];\n\n(* canonical names: factors sorted by shape \
(indices blanked), then indices numbered by first appearance \
*)\ncanonicalColour[network_] := Module[{factors = factorList[network], \
sorted, order},\n  sorted = SortBy[factors, {ToString[# /. {ColorT[l_, _, _] \
:> ColorT[Length[l], 0, 0], (h : ColorF | ColorDelta | GluonDelta)[x__] :> \
h[]}] &, ToString}];\n  order = DeleteDuplicates[Flatten[colourIndices /@ \
sorted]];\n  Times @@ sorted /. Thread[order -> Table[Symbol[\"colour\" <> \
ToString[n]], {n, Length[order]}]]];\n\n(* a network in generator strings; \
identity (1) for every f, factor by factor, so that each copy of a repeated f \
gets its own fresh indices *)\nfreshIndex[] := \
Unique[\"x\"];\nSetAttributes[adjointDelta, \
Orderless];\ntoGeneratorStrings[network_] := Times @@ (Replace[#, \
{ColorT[l_List, i_, j_] :> generators[l, i, j], ColorDelta[i_, j_] :> \
generators[{}, i, j], GluonDelta[a_, b_] :> adjointDelta[a, b],\n  ColorF[a_, \
b_, c_] :> With[{x = freshIndex[], y = freshIndex[]}, -2 I (generators[{a, b, \
c}, x, x] - generators[{b, a, c}, y, y])]}] & /@ factorList[network]);\n(* \
the reduction rules, in the order of the text above *)\ncolourRules = {\n  \
adjointDelta[a_, a_] :> Nc^2 - 1, adjointDelta[a_, b_]^2 :> Nc^2 - 1,\n  \
adjointDelta[a_, b_] adjointDelta[b_, c_] :> adjointDelta[a, c],\n  \
adjointDelta[a_, b_] generators[{x___, b_, y___}, i_, j_] :> generators[{x, \
a, y}, i, j],\n  generators[{}, i_, i_] :> Nc, generators[{_}, i_, i_] :> 0, \
generators[{}, i_, j_]^2 :> Nc,\n  generators[{}, i_, j_] generators[l_, i_, \
k_] :> generators[l, j, k], generators[{}, i_, j_] generators[l_, k_, j_] :> \
generators[l, k, i],\n  generators[l1_, i_, j_] generators[l2_, j_, k_] :> \
generators[Join[l1, l2], i, k],\n  generators[{x1___, a_, x2___, a_, x3___}, \
i_, j_] :> With[{z = freshIndex[]}, 1/2 (generators[{x2}, z, z] \
generators[{x1, x3}, i, j] - generators[{x1, x2, x3}, i, j]/Nc)],\n  \
generators[{x1___, a_, x2___}, i_, j_] generators[{y1___, a_, y2___}, k_, l_] \
:>\n    1/2 (generators[{x1, y2}, i, l] generators[{y1, x2}, k, j] - \
generators[{x1, x2}, i, j] generators[{y1, y2}, k, l]/Nc)};\ncolourCache = \
<||>;\ncolourValue[network_] := Module[{key = canonicalColour[network], \
value},\n  If[KeyExistsQ[colourCache, key], Return[colourCache[key]]];\n  \
value = Factor[FixedPoint[Expand[# /. colourRules] &, \
Expand[toGeneratorStrings[key]]]];\n  If[!FreeQ[value, generators | \
adjointDelta | colourHeads], Return[Failure[\"Colour\", <|\"Network\" -> key, \
\"Value\" -> value|>]]];\n  colourCache[key] = value];\n(* the colour sum of \
an amplitude structure c1 times the complex conjugate of c2 \
*)\ncolourSum[c1_, c2_] := colourValue[c1 conjugateColour[c2]];\n\"colour \
reduction defined\"", "Input"], Cell["Checks of the reduction on known colour \
sums (CF = (Nc^2-1)/(2 Nc)): Tr(T^a T^a) = CF Nc; f^{abc} f^{abc} = Nc \
(Nc^2-1); (T^a T^b)_{ij} ((T^a T^b)_{ij})^* = CF^2 Nc; (T^a T^b)_{ij} ((T^b \
T^a)_{ij})^* = -CF/2; f^{abc} (T^c)_{ij} ((T^a T^b)_{ij})^* = f^{abc} Tr[T^c \
T^b T^a] = -(i/4) f^{abc} f^{abc} = -i Nc (Nc^2-1)/4, which tests the sign of \
identity (1); the closed loop f^{a1 b1 c1} f^{a1 b2 c2} f^{b1 b2 d} f^{c1 c2 \
d} = Nc^2 (Nc^2-1)/2; and f^{z1 z2 z3} f^{z1 z2 z3}, which differs from the \
second network only by the names of its indices and must be found in the \
cache (the number of cached networks must not grow).  The full test of the \
colour algebra is the comparison of the Born squares with \
Processes/PartonicBorn below.", "Text"], Cell["colourTests = {\n  \
colourSum[ColorT[{a1}, i1, i2], ColorT[{a1}, i1, i2]] - (Nc^2 - 1)/2,\n  \
colourSum[ColorF[a1, a2, a3], ColorF[a1, a2, a3]] - Nc (Nc^2 - 1),\n  \
colourSum[ColorT[{a1, a2}, i1, i2], ColorT[{a1, a2}, i1, i2]] - Nc ((Nc^2 - \
1)/(2 Nc))^2,\n  colourSum[ColorT[{a1, a2}, i1, i2], ColorT[{a2, a1}, i1, \
i2]] + (Nc^2 - 1)/(4 Nc),\n  colourSum[ColorF[a1, a2, b] ColorT[{b}, i1, i2], \
ColorT[{a1, a2}, i1, i2]] + I Nc (Nc^2 - 1)/4,\n  colourValue[ColorF[a1, b1, \
c1] ColorF[a1, b2, c2] ColorF[b1, b2, d] ColorF[c1, c2, d]] - Nc^2 (Nc^2 - \
1)/2};\ncacheSize = Length[colourCache];\ncolourValue[ColorF[z1, z2, z3] \
ColorF[z1, z2, z3]];\nRequire[Simplify[colourTests] === {0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0} && \
Length[colourCache] === cacheSize, \"The colour reduction fails a known \
colour sum\", colourTests];\ncolourTests", "Input"], 
  Cell["From records to Tracer expressions", "Section"], 
  Cell["Each record becomes a Tracer expression: Metric[mu, nu] -> S[{mu}, \
{nu}], MomentumComponent[q, mu] -> S[q, {mu}], PolVector[l, mu, _] -> S[e_l, \
{mu}] with a vector e_l for the polarization of the gluon l (named epa, epb, \
ep, ek1, ek2; in the complex-conjugate amplitude epaStar, ...), Den[q] -> \
1/S[q, q] for a tree propagator (evaluated with the installed kinematics) or \
1/DjOf[q] for a propagator that carries the loop momentum (see the one-loop \
section).  An open fermion chain ubar(a) W u(b) becomes the inert object \
word[a, W..., b], with the spinor momenta at its ends and W the Tracer \
arguments ({mu} for gamma^mu, the momentum q for q-slash).  A closed quark \
loop becomes G[3, ...], a trace that Tracer evaluates at once, times its \
other factors.  The momenta inside the amplitude go through the map mom \
(momentum conservation, and for a one-loop graph also the shift of the loop \
momentum).  Because the record's factors are multiplied out, Tracer contracts \
every index summed inside the amplitude: indices of the metric tensors and \
momentum components disappear, and those attached to a fermion chain move \
into its word.", "Text"], Cell["polarization[l_] := Symbol[\"e\" <> \
ToString[l]];\npolarizationStar[l_] := Symbol[\"e\" <> ToString[l] <> \
\"Star\"];\nspinorMomentum[(Ubar | Vbar | Uspinor | Vspinor)[q_]] := \
q;\ntracerArgument[GammaMatrix[i_], mom_] := {i};\ntracerArgument[Slash[q_], \
mom_] := mom[q];\npropagator[q_] := If[FreeQ[q, loop], 1/S[q, q], \
1/DjOf[q]];\nclosedLoop[pieces_List, mom_] := Module[{gammas = Select[pieces, \
MatchQ[#, _GammaMatrix | _Slash] &]},\n  (Times @@ Select[pieces, !MatchQ[#, \
_GammaMatrix | _Slash] &]) If[gammas === {}, 1, G @@ Join[{3}, \
tracerArgument[#, mom] & /@ gammas]]];\nconvert[record_, mom_] := \
Module[{coefficient, words, loops},\n  coefficient = record[\"Coefficient\"] \
/. {Metric[i_, j_] :> S[{i}, {j}], MomentumComponent[q_, i_] :> S[mom[q], \
{i}],\n    PolVector[l_, i_, _] :> S[polarization[l], {i}], Den[q_] :> \
propagator[mom[q]]};\n  words = Times @@ (word @@ \
Join[{spinorMomentum[First[#]]}, tracerArgument[#, mom] & /@ (List @@ #)[[2 \
;; -2]], {spinorMomentum[Last[#]]}] & /@ record[\"Chains\"]);\n  loops = \
If[KeyExistsQ[record, \"Traces\"], Times @@ (closedLoop[List @@ #, mom] & /@ \
record[\"Traces\"]), 1];\n  Expand[coefficient words loops]];\n\"conversion \
defined\"", "Input"], Cell["The squaring method", "Section"], 
  Cell["As in the FeynCalc route, a square sum_{i,j} M_i M_j^* is not formed \
as one product:\n\n1. Every amplitude (one diagram) is converted and \
simplified once, before any product, and the conditions e_l.l = 0 and e_l.r = \
0 are imposed for every gluon l, where r is the reference vector of the same \
gluon's polarization sum (both the physical sum and the circular density are \
transverse to l and to r).  For the gluon whose momentum was eliminated by \
momentum conservation, e_x.x = 0 is imposed in its eliminated form: x = pa + \
pb - p (- k1) gives e_x.q = -(the other terms) for the first momentum q of x \
that is not its reference vector.\n2. Colour is separated from the Lorentz \
algebra: each amplitude is written as sum_x c_x L_x with distinct colour \
structures c_x; the colour factor of c_x c_y^* is computed by colourValue \
above.  The complex conjugate of a Lorentz part L_y changes i -> -i, e_l -> \
e_lStar, renames its summed Lorentz indices, and replaces each word ubar(a) W \
u(b) by its complex conjugate ubar(b) W^R u(a), with W^R the gamma string in \
reversed order (wordBar[b, W^R..., a]; reversing is the Dirac adjoint gamma0 \
W^dagger gamma0 of a string of gamma^mu and slashed momenta).\n3. Only the \
products with i <= j are computed: for i < j, M_i M_j^* + M_j M_i^* = 2 \
Re(M_i M_j^ (all invariants are real).\n4. The fermion lines are closed: in \
the product of the amplitude's words and the conjugate amplitude's words, the \
word that ends on the spinor of momentum q is followed by the conjugate word \
that starts there, with the spin sum in between: q-slash for u(q) ubar(q) and \
v(q) vbar(q) alike, and, for an incoming quark in the LL case, q-slash gamma5 \
times polarizedQuarkSign (+1 quark, -1 antiquark; gamma5 is placed directly \
after q-slash, and since q is four-dimensional this is the same as -gamma5 \
q-slash).  One continues with the next word until the first word comes back: \
each closed walk is one trace, trace[line, ...], kept inert for now.  The \
interference has one or two traces, depending on how the quark lines of the \
two diagrams connect.\n5. The gluon polarization sums are applied one gluon \
at a time, outgoing gluons first, before the traces are taken: the terms are \
grouped by the factors that carry that gluon's polarization vectors e_l and \
e_lStar; in each distinct group e_l -> {mu_l}, e_lStar -> {nu_l}, and the \
product with the density -g^{mu nu} + (l^mu r^nu + r^mu l^nu)/(l.r) (or, for \
a polarized incoming gluon, the circular density -i Eps[mu, nu, l, r]/(2 \
l.r)) is expanded once, Tracer contracting the indices, also into the inert \
traces.  Contracting before tracing keeps the traces short: a contracted pair \
gamma^mu ... gamma_mu inside a trace is reduced by Tracer's D-dimensional \
contraction formulas before the trace is expanded.  (Tracer does not move an \
index of Eps into a trace, so the two indices of a circular density stay free \
in the trace and are contracted with Eps after it.)\n6. The traces are then \
evaluated (each distinct one once) and the products expanded; every remaining \
scalar product is a kinematic invariant.  An epsilon tensor of the eliminated \
momentum is rewritten with momentum conservation.  The products (i, j) are \
independent: they run on parallel kernels, and each is written to its own \
file with the time it took, so that the progress is visible and an \
interrupted run can be continued.", "Text"], Cell["(* ---- 1. one amplitude, \
with the transversality conditions ---- *)\ntransversality[references_, \
conservation_] := Module[{x = conservation[[1]], momenta, solved, \
coefficient},\n  momenta = Cases[termList[Expand[conservation[[2]]]], c_. \
q_Symbol :> q];\n  solved = First[DeleteCases[momenta, references[x]]];\n  \
coefficient[q_] := Coefficient[conservation[[2]], q];\n  {{S[polarization[x], \
solved] -> -Sum[coefficient[q] S[polarization[x], q], {q, \
DeleteCases[momenta, solved]}]/coefficient[solved]},\n   \
Flatten[Table[{S[polarization[l], l] -> 0, S[polarization[l], references[l]] \
-> 0}, {l, Keys[references]}]]}];\nprepare[diagram_, references_, \
conservation_, mom_] := Module[{a = Total[convert[#, mom] & /@ diagram], \
rules = transversality[references, conservation]},\n  Expand[Expand[a /. \
rules[[1]]] /. rules[[2]]]];\n\n(* ---- 2. colour separation and complex \
conjugation ---- *)\ncolourPart[term_] := Times @@ Select[factorList[term], \
!FreeQ[#, colourHeads] &];\n(* {{c_x, L_x}, ...}: the distinct colour \
structures of an amplitude with their Lorentz parts *)\ncolourGroups[amp_] := \
Module[{groups = GatherBy[termList[Expand[amp]], colourPart]},\n  \
Table[{colourPart[First[g]], Total[(#/colourPart[#]) & /@ g]}, {g, \
groups}]];\nlorentzIndices[expr_] := Union[Cases[expr, {i_Symbol} /; \
StringStartsQ[SymbolName[i], \"Lor\"] :> i, Infinity]];    (* FeynArts names \
them Lor1, Lor2, ... *)\ngluonsOf[expr_] := Union[Cases[expr, s_Symbol /; \
StringMatchQ[SymbolName[s], \"e\" ~~ (\"pa\" | \"pb\" | \"p\" | \"k1\" | \
\"k2\")] :> ToExpression[StringDrop[SymbolName[s], 1]], \
Infinity]];\nconjugateLorentz[lorentz_] := Module[{gluons = \
gluonsOf[lorentz], indices = lorentzIndices[lorentz]},\n  lorentz /. \
Thread[polarization /@ gluons -> polarizationStar /@ gluons] /. \
Thread[indices -> (Symbol[\"c\" <> SymbolName[#]] & /@ indices)] /.\n    \
{Complex[x_, y_] :> Complex[x, -y], word[a_, w___, b_] :> wordBar[b, Sequence \
@@ Reverse[{w}], a]}];\nconjugateGroups[amp_] := {conjugateColour[#[[1]]], \
conjugateLorentz[#[[2]]]} & /@ colourGroups[amp];\n\n(* ---- 4. closing the \
fermion lines ---- *)\n(* the spin sum at the spinor of momentum q: {Tracer \
arguments, sign} *)\njunction[q_, spinCase_] := If[spinCase === \"LL\" && \
MemberQ[incomingQuarks, q], {{q, G5}, polarizedQuarkSign[q]}, {{q}, \
1}];\nsew[term_, spinCase_] := Module[{factors = factorList[term], words, \
bars, rest, traces = {}, sign = 1, current, start, chain, q, j},\n  words = \
Association[#[[1]] -> # & /@ Cases[factors, _word]];          (* each word, \
keyed by the momentum it starts with *)\n  bars = Association[#[[1]] -> # & \
/@ Cases[factors, _wordBar]];        (* each conjugate word, keyed likewise \
*)\n  rest = Times @@ DeleteCases[factors, _word | _wordBar];\n  \
While[Length[words] > 0,\n    current = First[words]; start = current[[1]]; \
chain = {};\n    While[True,\n      KeyDropFrom[words, current[[1]]];\n      \
q = Last[current]; chain = Join[chain, List @@ current[[2 ;; -2]]];\n      j \
= junction[q, spinCase]; chain = Join[chain, j[[1]]]; sign *= j[[2]];\n      \
Require[KeyExistsQ[bars, q], \"A fermion line does not close\", term];\n      \
current = bars[q]; q = Last[current]; chain = Join[chain, List @@ current[[2 \
;; -2]]];\n      j = junction[q, spinCase]; chain = Join[chain, j[[1]]]; sign \
*= j[[2]];\n      If[q === start, Break[]];\n      Require[KeyExistsQ[words, \
q], \"A fermion line does not close\", term];\n      current = words[q]];\n   \
 AppendTo[traces, trace @@ Join[{Length[traces] + 1}, chain]]];\n  sign rest \
Times @@ traces];\n\n(* ---- 5. polarization sums ---- *)\nphysicalSum[l_, \
r_] := With[{mu = {Symbol[\"mu\" <> ToString[l]]}, nu = {Symbol[\"nu\" <> \
ToString[l]]}},\n  -S[mu, nu] + (S[l, mu] S[r, nu] + S[r, mu] S[l, nu])/S[l, \
r]];\ncircular[l_, r_] := With[{mu = {Symbol[\"mu\" <> ToString[l]]}, nu = \
{Symbol[\"nu\" <> ToString[l]]}},\n  -I Eps[mu, nu, l, r]/(2 S[l, r])];       \
                   (* Tracer's sign of Eps, see the introduction \
*)\ntensorPart[term_, l_] := Times @@ Select[factorList[term], !FreeQ[#, \
polarization[l] | polarizationStar[l]] &];\n(* the contraction uses the \
installed scalar products, which differ between the Born and the real \
kinematics: the kinematics are part of the key *)\nprojectionCache = <||>; \
currentKinematics = None;\nprojectOnce[tensor_, l_, density_] := With[{key = \
{currentKinematics, tensor, density}},\n  If[KeyExistsQ[projectionCache, \
key], projectionCache[key],\n    With[{value = Expand[(tensor /. \
{polarization[l] -> {Symbol[\"mu\" <> ToString[l]]}, polarizationStar[l] -> \
{Symbol[\"nu\" <> ToString[l]]}}) density]},\n      If[FreeQ[tensor, trace], \
projectionCache[key] = value, value]]]];     (* tensors with traces are \
rarely repeated: not stored *)\nproject[expr_, l_, density_] := If[expr === \
0, 0, Module[{groups = GatherBy[termList[expr], tensorPart[#, l] &]},\n  \
Require[And @@ (!FreeQ[#, polarization[l]] && !FreeQ[#, polarizationStar[l]] \
& /@ groups[[All, 1]]), \"A term lacks a polarization vector\", l];\n  \
Expand[Total[Table[With[{tensor = tensorPart[First[g], l]}, Total[(#/tensor) \
& /@ g] projectOnce[tensor, l, density]], {g, groups}]]]]];\n\n(* ---- 6. \
traces ---- *)\nevaluateTraces[expr_] := Module[{cache = <||>},\n  \
Expand[expr /. trace[n_, a___] :> Lookup[cache, Key[{n, a}], cache[{n, a}] = \
Expand[G[n, a]]]]];\n\n(* one product (i, j): left = {{c_x, L_x}, ...} of the \
amplitude, right = {{c_y^*, L_y^*}, ...} of the conjugate amplitude \
*)\ninterference[left_, right_, spinCase_, references_, conservation_] := \
Module[{product, gluons, expr},\n  product = \
Expand[Total[Flatten[Table[colourValue[x[[1]] y[[1]]] x[[2]] y[[2]], {x, \
left}, {y, right}]]]];\n  If[!FreeQ[product, Failure], \
Return[FirstCase[product, _Failure, Null, Infinity]]];\n  If[product === 0, \
Return[0]];          (* a graph can vanish once e_l.l = e_l.r = 0 are imposed \
*)\n  gluons = gluonsOf[{left[[All, 2]]}];\n  expr = Expand[Total[sew[#, \
spinCase] & /@ termList[product]]];\n  Do[expr = project[expr, l, \
physicalSum[l, references[l]]], {l, Complement[gluons, {pa, pb}]}];       (* \
outgoing gluons first *)\n  Do[expr = project[expr, l, If[spinCase === \
\"LL\", circular[l, references[l]], physicalSum[l, references[l]]]], {l, \
Intersection[gluons, {pa, pb}]}];\n  expr = evaluateTraces[expr];\n  (* the \
eliminated momentum inside a four-dimensional epsilon tensor (in the Born \
kinematics Eps[pa, pb, p, k1] = 0) *)\n  Expand[expr /. epsHead[x_List] :> \
(Eps @@ (x /. conservation))]];\n(* the real part: after expanding, every \
term is a number times real symbols (the denominators are real propagators), \
so the real part of the number is kept *)\nrealPartOf[expr_] := Expand[expr] \
/. Complex[a_, b_] :> a;\nimaginaryPartOf[expr_] := (expr - (expr /. \
Complex[a_, b_] :> Complex[a, -b]))/2;\n\"squaring functions defined\"", 
   "Input"], Cell["Parallel kernels (choice workers above): each loads \
FeynFacet and Tracer (Tracer works in parallel kernels).", "Text"], 
  Cell["feynFacetFile = FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"..\", \"..\", \
\"FeynFacet\", \"FeynFacet.wl\"}];\nnWorkers = If[workers === \"auto\", \
Min[$ProcessorCount, 8], ToExpression[workers]];   (* \"auto\": one per \
processor core, at most 8 *)\nIf[nWorkers > 1,\n  LaunchKernels[nWorkers];\n  \
With[{file = feynFacetFile}, ParallelEvaluate[Get[file]; \
LoadTracer[]]]];\n\"parallel kernels: \" <> ToString[Max[1, \
Length[Kernels[]]]]", "Input"], Cell["Each parallel kernel sets the \
dimension, the HVBM gamma5 and the traced lines, and receives the functions \
above with empty caches.  A job is one product (i, j) of the squaring method: \
it installs its kinematics (Born or real) inside Internal`InheritedBlock, \
computes the interference, and is written to \
Results/Tracer/class-<n>/pairs/<name>.wl with its time.  square adds the \
products of one square: a diagonal product as it is, a product with i < j \
twice its real part (step 3).  A diagonal product |M_i|^2 is real, but its \
epsilon-tensor terms may leave an imaginary part that vanishes only after \
simplification: that imaginary part is checked to be exactly zero at a \
rational point (checkPoint) and dropped.  sidesOf prepares every diagram once \
in the given kinematics, separates its colour, and forms its conjugate.", 
   "Text"], Cell["If[nWorkers > 1,\n  ParallelEvaluate[VectorDimension[D]; \
AntiCommute[off]; Spur[1, 2, 3]];\n  DistributeDefinitions[declare, \
fourDimensional, bornKinematics, realKinematics, installKinematics, \
epsHead,\n    colourHeads, factorList, termList, colourIndices, \
internalColour, conjugateColour, canonicalColour, freshIndex, adjointDelta, \
toGeneratorStrings, colourRules, colourValue,\n    polarization, \
polarizationStar, junction, sew, physicalSum, circular, tensorPart, \
projectOnce, project, evaluateTraces, gluonsOf, interference,\n    \
incomingQuarks, incomingGluons, polarizedQuarkSign];\n  \
ParallelEvaluate[colourCache = <||>; projectionCache = <||>; \
currentKinematics = None]];\npairDirectory = \
FileNameJoin[{ResultsDirectory[\"Tracer/class-\" <> class], \
\"pairs\"}];\nIf[!DirectoryQ[pairDirectory], \
CreateDirectory[pairDirectory]];\n(* the fingerprint of the inputs of the \
product files: the amplitudes of step 1 and this step file (see the choice \
resume above) *)\ninputFingerprint = InputFingerprint[loaded, \
{FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \
\"2-Algebra-Tracer.wl\"}]}];\nrunJob[job_] := Module[{file = \
FileNameJoin[{pairDirectory, job[\"Name\"] <> \".wl\"}], value, seconds},\n  \
If[resume === \"yes\" && ReusableQ[file, inputFingerprint], file,\n    \
{seconds, value} = AbsoluteTiming[Internal`InheritedBlock[{S, H}, \
installKinematics[job[\"Kinematics\"]]; currentKinematics = \
job[\"Kinematics\"];\n      interference[job[\"Left\"], job[\"Right\"], \
job[\"Spin\"], job[\"References\"], job[\"Conservation\"]]]];\n    \
If[!FreeQ[value, Failure], value,\n      Put[<|\"Name\" -> job[\"Name\"], \
\"Value\" -> value, \"Seconds\" -> seconds|>, file]; MarkReusable[file, \
inputFingerprint]]]];\nrunJobs[jobs_] := Module[{files},\n  If[nWorkers > 1, \
DistributeDefinitions[runJob, pairDirectory, resume, inputFingerprint]];\n  \
files = If[nWorkers > 1, ParallelMap[runJob, jobs, Method -> \
\"FinestGrained\"], Map[runJob, jobs]];\n  Require[FreeQ[files, Failure], \"A \
job failed\", FirstCase[files, _Failure, Null, Infinity]];\n  Get /@ \
files];\n(* ---- 3. the pairs i <= j of a square, and their sum ---- \
*)\nsquareJobs[name_, sides_, kinematics_, references_, conservation_, \
spinCase_] := Flatten[Table[\n  <|\"Name\" -> name <> \"-\" <> spinCase <> \
\"-\" <> ToString[i] <> \"-\" <> ToString[j], \"Kinematics\" -> kinematics,\n \
   \"Left\" -> sides[[1, i]], \"Right\" -> sides[[2, j]], \"Spin\" -> \
spinCase, \"References\" -> references, \"Conservation\" -> conservation, \
\"Pair\" -> {i, j}|>,\n  {i, Length[sides[[1]]]}, {j, i, \
Length[sides[[1]]]}]];\ncheckPoint = {s -> 1, t -> -3/10, u -> -2/5, A -> \
-1/7, B -> -2/9, C -> -3/10 + 1/7 + 2/9, D -> 37/10, Nc -> 3, spe3 -> 1/11, \
gs -> 1, Nf -> 5};\nsquare[name_, sides_, kinematics_, references_, \
conservation_, spinCase_] := Module[{jobs = squareJobs[name, sides, \
kinematics, references, conservation, spinCase], results},\n  results = \
runJobs[jobs];\n  Require[And @@ MapThread[#2[\"Pair\"][[1]] != \
#2[\"Pair\"][[2]] || (imaginaryPartOf[#1[\"Value\"]] /. checkPoint) === 0 &, \
{results, jobs}],\n    \"A diagonal product has a nonzero imaginary part\", \
name];\n  Total[MapThread[If[#2[\"Pair\"][[1]] == #2[\"Pair\"][[2]], \
realPartOf[#1[\"Value\"]], 2 realPartOf[#1[\"Value\"]]] &, {results, \
jobs}]]];\nsidesOf[diagrams_, kinematics_, references_, conservation_] := \
Module[{prepared},\n  prepared = Internal`InheritedBlock[{S, H}, \
installKinematics[kinematics];\n    prepare[#, references, conservation, \
conservedMomentum[conservation]] & /@ diagrams];\n  {colourGroups /@ \
prepared, conjugateGroups /@ prepared}];\n\"jobs defined\"", "Input"], 
  Cell["Born", "Section"], Cell["The Born square with the reference vectors \
of the FeynCalc route: pa -> pb, pb -> pa (incoming gluons), p -> pa, k1 -> \
pa; averaged over the incoming spins and colours, and written with CA, CF and \
u = -s - t.  No identical-particle factor: the tagged parton p is \
distinguished from the unobserved one.", "Text"], 
  Cell["bornReferences = <|pa -> pb, pb -> pa, p -> pa, k1 -> \
pa|>;\nbornSides = If[records[\"Born\"] === {}, None, \
sidesOf[records[\"Born\"], \"Born\", bornReferences, \
bornConservation]];\nborn = If[bornSides === None, <|\"UU\" -> 0, \"LL\" -> \
0|>,\n  Association @ Table[spinCase -> With[{sq = square[\"born\", \
bornSides, \"Born\", bornReferences, bornConservation, spinCase]},\n    \
Factor[colourFactors[Together[average[spinCase] sq]] /. u -> -s - t]], \
{spinCase, {\"UU\", \"LL\"}}]];\nRequire[FreeQ[born, Complex | S | H | \
epsHead | trace | word | wordBar], \"The Born square is not a real scalar\", \
born];\nborn", "Input"], Cell["The Born squares must agree with the table of \
Processes/PartonicBorn (checked against the textbook); this tests the colour \
reduction, the closing of the fermion lines, the gluon sums and the signs of \
the polarized densities.", "Text"], Cell["(* the table is read only for a \
class with a Born term (the classes without one do not need \
Processes/PartonicBorn here) *)\nIf[spec[\"Born\"] =!= None,\n  bornTable = \
Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"..\", \"PartonicBorn\", \"Results\", \
\"Born.wl\"}]];\n  Require[And @@ Table[Simplify[born[sc]/gs^4 - \
bornTable[\"Born\"][sc][StringRiffle[spec[\"Born\"][[1 ;; 2]], \" \"] <> \" \
-> \" <> spec[\"Born\"][[3]]]] === 0, {sc, {\"UU\", \"LL\"}}],\n    \"The \
Born square differs from Processes/PartonicBorn\", born]];\n\"Born checked\""\
, "Input"], 
  Cell["Virtual: the one-loop interference in terms of scalar integrals", 
   "Section"], Cell["The families, the routing of the loop momentum and the \
reduction of the loop momentum's scalar products are those of the FeynCalc \
route:\n\n   VirtualST[n1,n2,n3,n4]: 1/[(loop^2)^n1 ((loop+pa)^2)^n2 \
((loop+pa+pb)^2)^n3 ((loop+p)^2)^n4]   (external legs pa, pb, -pd, -p in \
cyclic order: invariants s and t),\n   VirtualSU: ... ((loop+pa+pb)^2)^n3 \
((loop+pa+pb-p)^2)^n4   (legs pa, pb, -p, -pd: s and u),      VirtualTU: \
((loop+pa)^2)^n2 ((loop+pa-p)^2)^n3 ((loop+pa-p+pb)^2)^n4   (legs pa, -p, pb, \
-pd: t and u),\n\nwith negative indices for numerators.  FeynArts routes the \
loop momentum differently in every graph; for every graph the routing loop -> \
sigma loop + delta (sigma = +-1) that maps its loop propagators onto one \
family is found by trying the shifts, the same search in the same order as in \
the FeynCalc route.", "Text"], Cell["families = <|\n  \"VirtualST\" -> {loop, \
loop + pa, loop + pa + pb, loop + p},                 (* legs pa, pb, -pd, -p \
in cyclic order: invariants s and t *)\n  \"VirtualSU\" -> {loop, loop + pa, \
loop + pa + pb, loop + pa + pb - p},       (* legs pa, pb, -p, -pd: s and u \
*)\n  \"VirtualTU\" -> {loop, loop + pa, loop + pa - p, loop + pa - p + \
pb}|>;      (* legs pa, -p, pb, -pd: t and u *)\nfamilyHeads = \
<|\"VirtualST\" -> KVirtualST, \"VirtualSU\" -> KVirtualSU, \"VirtualTU\" -> \
KVirtualTU|>;\nshifts = Flatten[Table[c1 pa + c2 pb + c3 p, {c1, -1, 1}, {c2, \
-1, 1}, {c3, -1, 1}]];\npropagatorMomenta[diagram_] := Union[Cases[diagram, \
Den[q_] /; !FreeQ[q, loop] :> Expand[q /. bornConservation], Infinity]];   (* \
the loop propagators *)\nsameUpToSign[q1_, q2_] := Expand[q1 - q2] === 0 || \
Expand[q1 + q2] === 0;\n(* find sigma, delta and the family such that every \
loop propagator of the graph, with loop -> sigma loop + delta, is one of the \
family's *)\nrouting[diagram_] := Module[{props = propagatorMomenta[diagram], \
found},\n  found = Catch[Do[If[And @@ Table[Or @@ Table[sameUpToSign[q /. \
loop -> sigma loop + delta, f], {f, families[name]}], {q, props}],\n      \
Throw[{name, sigma, delta}]], {name, Keys[families]}, {sigma, {1, -1}}, \
{delta, shifts}]; None];\n  Require[found =!= None, \"No family fits the \
propagators of a one-loop graph\", props]; found];\nroutings = routing /@ \
records[\"Virtual\"];\nCounts[routings[[All, 1]]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["For each graph: convert it with the map mom = (shift of the loop \
momentum, then k1 -> pa + pb - p), so that each loop propagator becomes \
1/DjOf[q] with q one of the family's momenta up to sign (a tree propagator \
next to the loop is evaluated); prepare it once and separate its colour; its \
products with the conjugate of the summed Born amplitude are the jobs below \
(one per graph and spin case).\n\nAfter the spin sums and the traces the loop \
momentum appears only through S[loop, loop], S[loop, pa], S[loop, pb], \
S[loop, p] (S[loop, k1], from the spin sum of an outgoing quark k1, is \
rewritten with k1 = pa + pb - p) and the hatted H[loop, loop] = loopHat2.  \
Tracer's S is D-dimensional and H its (D-4)-dimensional part, so no \
four-dimensional product needs to be rewritten (in the FeynCalc route \
loop4.loop4 = loop.loop - loopHat2 is substituted).  The four D-dimensional \
products are expressed through the inverse propagators Dj of the family (the \
four equations loop^2 = D1, 2 loop.q_j = D_j - D_1 - q_j^2 are solved for \
loop^2, loop.pa, loop.pb, loop.p), and each term is read off as coefficient x \
family[indices] x HatPower[n].  loopHat2 shifts the dimension of the integral \
in step 3, not the dimension D of the coefficients.", "Text"], 
  Cell["loopProducts = {L2 -> S[loop, loop], Lpa -> S[loop, pa], Lpb -> \
S[loop, pb], Lp -> S[loop, p]};\ninverseProps[name_] := Module[{q = \
families[name], sol},\n  sol = Internal`InheritedBlock[{S, H}, \
bornKinematics;\n    Solve[Table[Dj[j] == Expand[S[q[[j]], q[[j]]]] /. \
Reverse /@ loopProducts, {j, 4}] /. u -> -s - t, {L2, Lpa, Lpb, Lp}]];\n  \
Require[Length[sol] == 1, \"Cannot express the loop scalar products through \
the propagators\"]; First[sol]];\nloopRules[name_] := loopRules[name] = \
With[{sol = inverseProps[name]}, Table[(x /. loopProducts) -> (x /. sol), {x, \
{L2, Lpa, Lpb, Lp}}]];\nshiftedMomentum[{name_, sigma_, delta_}][q_] := \
Expand[q /. loop -> sigma loop + delta /. bornConservation];\n(* the \
contracted interference of one graph -> sum of coefficient x family[indices] \
x HatPower[n] *)\ntoFamilies[expr0_, name_] := Module[{expr},\n  expr = \
Expand[expr0 /. S[loop, k1] :> S[loop, pa + pb - p] /. H[loop, loop] -> \
loopHat2 /. loopRules[name]];\n  Require[FreeQ[expr /. _DjOf -> 1, loop], \"A \
product of the loop momentum was not expressed through the propagators\",\n   \
 Short[Union[Cases[expr, h_[a___] /; !FreeQ[{a}, loop] && FreeQ[h, Times | \
Plus | Power | DjOf], Infinity]], 8]];\n  expr = Expand[expr /. DjOf[q_] :> \
Dj @@ (Position[families[name], f_ /; sameUpToSign[f, q]][[1]])];\n  (* every \
term is a coefficient times powers of the Dj (negative for propagators, \
positive for numerators) and of loopHat2 *)\n  Total[Table[With[{powers = \
Table[Exponent[term, Dj[j]], {j, 4}], hat = Exponent[term, loopHat2]},\n    \
(term/(Times @@ Table[Dj[j]^powers[[j]], {j, 4}] loopHat2^hat)) \
familyHeads[name] @@ (-powers) HatPower[hat]], {term, \
DeleteCases[termList[expr], 0]}]]];\nvirtualLeft = \
Internal`InheritedBlock[{S, H}, bornKinematics;\n  \
MapThread[colourGroups[prepare[#1, bornReferences, bornConservation, \
shiftedMomentum[#2]]] &, {records[\"Virtual\"], routings}]];\nbornSumRight = \
If[records[\"Born\"] === {}, {}, Internal`InheritedBlock[{S, H}, \
bornKinematics;\n  conjugateGroups[Total[prepare[#, bornReferences, \
bornConservation, conservedMomentum[bornConservation]] & /@ \
records[\"Born\"]]]]];\nLength[virtualLeft]", "Input"], 
  Cell["The interference 2 Re(M1 M0, normalized as in the FeynCalc route.  \
FeynArts writes the one-loop amplitude with the measure d^D loop/(2 Pi)^D; \
the scalar integrals are defined with the measure d^D loop/(i Pi^(D/2)), so \
that M1 = i/(4 Pi)^(D/2) x (sum of coefficients c_j times integrals I_j).  \
The products (coefficient x M0 formed by the spin sums are real, and\n\n   2 \
Re(M1 M0 = (2/(4 Pi)^(D/2)) Sum_j [i c_j M0*] Re(I_j),\n\nwith the real parts \
of the integrals in the physical region (s > 0) taken in step 3.  The \
association virtual below holds Sum_j [i c_j M0*] I_j, averaged, for both \
spin cases, with the loop-momentum hat powers as HatPower[n]; the factor 2/(4 \
Pi)^(D/2) is included in step 4.", "Text"], Cell["virtualJobs[spinCase_] := \
Table[<|\"Name\" -> \"virtual-\" <> spinCase <> \"-\" <> ToString[g], \
\"Kinematics\" -> \"Born\", \"Left\" -> virtualLeft[[g]],\n  \"Right\" -> \
bornSumRight, \"Spin\" -> spinCase, \"References\" -> bornReferences, \
\"Conservation\" -> bornConservation|>, {g, Length[virtualLeft]}];\nvirtual = \
If[records[\"Virtual\"] === {}, <|\"UU\" -> 0, \"LL\" -> 0|>,\n  Association \
@ Table[spinCase -> Module[{results = runJobs[virtualJobs[spinCase]]},\n    \
Collect[I average[spinCase] Total[MapThread[toFamilies[#1[\"Value\"], \
#2[[1]]] &, {results, routings}]] /. u -> -s - t,\n      {_KVirtualST, \
_KVirtualSU, _KVirtualTU, _HatPower}, colourFactors]], {spinCase, {\"UU\", \
\"LL\"}}]];\nRequire[FreeQ[virtual, Complex | S | H | epsHead | trace], \"The \
virtual interference is not a real combination of scalar integrals\", \
virtual];\n{Length[virtual[\"UU\"]], Union[Cases[virtual, (KVirtualST | \
KVirtualSU | KVirtualTU)[__], Infinity]] // Length}", "Input"], 
  Cell["Real emission", "Section"], Cell["For every real-emission process of \
the class, the square of the sum of its diagrams with the spin sums of the \
two cases, in terms of s, t, u, A, B, C and spe3; the processes are added \
with their weights from classes.wl, which also carry the identical-particle \
factors (1/2 for two identical unobserved gluons; 1 when the tagged parton \
has an identical unobserved partner, since the two ways of tagging cancel the \
1/2; Nf - 1 or Nf for a quark pair of other flavours).  Reference vectors: pa \
for the gluons p and k1, pb for k2, the other incoming momentum for an \
incoming gluon.  In the real kinematics a four-dimensional epsilon tensor \
Eps[pa, pb, p, k1] can appear (k1 has a four-dimensional part out of the \
plane of pa, pb, p); it always comes with an imaginary coefficient and drops \
out of the real part, which the checks at the end of the cell below confirm.  \
The sum over processes is not brought to a common denominator (step 3 expands \
it into partial fractions anyway).", "Text"], Cell["realReferences = <|pa -> \
pb, pb -> pa, p -> pa, k1 -> pa, k2 -> pb|>;\nrealSides = Association @ \
KeyValueMap[#1 -> sidesOf[#2, \"Real\", realReferences, realConservation] &, \
records[\"Real\"]];\nrealSquares = Association @ Table[spinCase -> \
Association @ KeyValueMap[\n    #1 -> square[\"real-\" <> StringReplace[#1, \
\" \" -> \"_\"], #2, \"Real\", realReferences, realConservation, spinCase] &, \
realSides], {spinCase, {\"UU\", \"LL\"}}];\nreal = Association @ \
Table[spinCase -> (average[spinCase] Total[KeyValueMap[weights[#1] #2 &, \
realSquares[spinCase]]] /. Nc -> CA),\n  {spinCase, {\"UU\", \
\"LL\"}}];\nRequire[FreeQ[real, Complex], \"The real-emission square is not \
real\"];\nRequire[FreeQ[real, S | H | epsHead | trace | word | wordBar | \
List], \"A scalar product or tensor was left in the real-emission square\", \
Union[Cases[real, _S | _H | _epsHead, Infinity]]];\nRequire[Max[Exponent[#, \
spe3] & /@ termList[Expand[real[\"LL\"]]]] <= 1, \"The real-emission square \
has spe3^2 terms\"];\nLeafCount /@ real", "Input"], 
  Cell["Check of the gauge invariance of the real-emission square, as in the \
FeynCalc route: for the first process of the class (spin average), the \
physical polarization sums with other reference vectors (pb for p and k1, pa \
for k2) give the same result.  The amplitudes are prepared again, since the \
conditions e_l.r = 0 depend on the reference vectors.  The difference is \
evaluated exactly at random rational points (all invariants, D, Nc and spe3), \
with C = -s4 - A - B.", "Text"], Cell["alternativeReferences = <|pa -> pb, pb \
-> pa, p -> pb, k1 -> pb, k2 -> pa|>;\nfirstProcess = \
First[Keys[records[\"Real\"]]];\nalternative = square[\"gauge-\" <> \
StringReplace[firstProcess, \" \" -> \"_\"],\n  \
sidesOf[records[\"Real\"][firstProcess], \"Real\", alternativeReferences, \
realConservation], \"Real\", alternativeReferences, realConservation, \
\"UU\"];\ngaugePoints = Table[With[{v = RandomInteger[{1, 97}, \
7]/RandomInteger[{98, 197}, 7]},\n  {s -> 1, t -> -v[[1]], u -> -v[[2]] (1 - \
v[[1]]), A -> -v[[3]], B -> -v[[4]], D -> 4 - v[[5]], Nc -> 2 + 10 v[[6]], \
spe3 -> v[[7]]}], {3}];\nreferenceDifference = Table[(alternative - \
realSquares[\"UU\"][firstProcess]) /. C -> -(s + t + u) - A - B /. point, \
{point, gaugePoints}];\nRequire[referenceDifference === {0, 0, 0}, \"The \
real-emission square depends on the gluon reference vectors\", \
referenceDifference];\n\"gauge invariance of the real emission checked\"", 
   "Input"], Cell["Timing and save", "Section"], 
  Cell["The number of products computed, and their total and largest time in \
seconds (from the pair files).", "Text"], Cell["pairTimes = Association @ \
Table[FileBaseName[f] -> Get[f][\"Seconds\"], {f, FileNames[\"*.wl\", \
pairDirectory]}];\n{Length[pairTimes], Round[Total[pairTimes]], \
Round[Max[pairTimes]]}", "Input"], Cell["The result, in the format of the \
FeynCalc route, is saved to Results/Tracer/class-<n>/Algebra.wl, and the \
parallel kernels are closed.", "Text"], Cell["algebra = <|\"Born\" -> born, \
\"Virtual\" -> virtual, \"Real\" -> real, \"Class\" -> class, \"Spec\" -> \
spec,\n  \"Families\" -> families, \"Variables\" -> \"s, t, u = -s-t; A = \
(pa-k1)^2, B = (pb-k1)^2, C = (p+k1)^2 = -s4-A-B; spe3; loopHat2 via \
HatPower[n]\"|>;\nSaveResult[\"Algebra\", algebra, \"Tracer/class-\" <> \
class];\nCloseKernels[];\nKeys[algebra]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Comparison with the FeynCalc route", "Section"], 
  Cell["The two routes must give the same Algebra.wl.  Born, virtual and real \
parts are compared, in exact arithmetic, at two random rational points (a \
sampled comparison, not a symbolic identity) of s, t, u, A, B, D, CA, spe3 \
and Nf, with C = -(s+t+u) - A - B and CF = (CA^2-1)/(2 CA); in the virtual \
part every scalar integral K...[n1,n2,n3,n4] is replaced by its own random \
rational number and HatPower[n] by hp^n with a random rational hp, so that \
the coefficient of every integral and every hat power is compared.  (If the \
FeynCalc route has not been run for this class, the comparison is skipped and \
says so.)", "Text"], Cell["feynCalcFile = \
FileNameJoin[{ResultsDirectory[\"FeynCalc/class-\" <> class], \
\"Algebra.wl\"}];\ncomparison = If[!FileExistsQ[feynCalcFile], \"FeynCalc \
result not available: comparison skipped\",\n  Module[{other = \
Get[feynCalcFile], integrals, points, valueAt},\n    integrals = \
Union[Cases[{virtual, other[\"Virtual\"]}, (KVirtualST | KVirtualSU | \
KVirtualTU)[__], Infinity]];\n    points = Table[Join[With[{v = \
RandomInteger[{1, 997}, 9]/RandomInteger[{998, 1997}, 9]},\n        {s -> 1 + \
v[[1]], t -> -v[[2]], u -> -v[[3]], A -> -v[[4]], B -> -v[[5]], D -> 4 - \
v[[6]], CA -> 2 + 10 v[[7]], spe3 -> v[[8]], Nf -> 1 + 5 v[[9]], hp -> 1 + \
v[[1]] v[[2]]}],\n      Thread[integrals -> RandomInteger[{1, 10^6}, \
Length[integrals]]/RandomInteger[{1, 10^6}, Length[integrals]]]], {2}];\n    \
valueAt[expr_, point_] := expr /. HatPower[n_] :> hp^n /. point /. C -> -(s + \
t + u) - A - B /. CF -> (CA^2 - 1)/(2 CA) /. point;\n    Association @ \
Flatten[Table[part <> \" \" <> sc -> \
Union[Table[Together[valueAt[algebra[part][sc], point] - \
valueAt[other[part][sc], point]], {point, points}]],\n      {part, {\"Born\", \
\"Virtual\", \"Real\"}}, {sc, {\"UU\", \
\"LL\"}}]]]];\nRequire[!AssociationQ[comparison] || \
Union[Flatten[Values[comparison]]] === {0}, \"The Tracer route differs from \
the FeynCalc route\", comparison];\ncomparison", "Input"]}, 
 WindowSize -> {1000, 800}]
